{"id": "EUVD-2026-102327", "enisaUuid": "b73f1074-596b-3414-8a06-bc6f6fea8714", "description": "Netgate pfSense CE through 2.9.0 contains an OS command injection vulnerability that allows authenticated users to execute commands as root by supplying a crafted wireless parent interface name. Attackers with limited Wireless Edit or Interface Assignments privileges can submit values like ath0;<cmd> via interfaces_wireless_edit.php or interfaces_assign.php, which interface_wireless_clone() interpolates unescaped into an ifconfig shell command.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:43:31", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-wireless-clone", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-assign-if-add", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/interfaces.inc#L3370", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/interfaces_wireless_edit.php#L77", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/interfaces_assign.php#L187", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-through-2.9.0-os-command-injection-via-wireless-parent-interface"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111215", "GHSA-qcp6-4768-v6qq"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 6.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d6a5d071-5e63-390c-ba8d-6683459cfa04", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "91314b4b-4449-35f3-8012-323d60b90222", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}